  "narrative": "Round 2 discovery evidence identifies two important dataset-specific signals and several null broad probes. H27 is the strongest result: within the high feature_036 subgroup, feature_003 positivity is associated with a lower composite dependency score by 0.443 units signed to the claimed negative-direction claim, and the entire 95% interval is above the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept H27 as a dataset-specific association, while retaining active status because it emerged from exploratory subgroup testing and requires independent reproducibility; I request validation of H27. H26 and H25, the corresponding high feature_038 and high feature_018 strata, have point estimates above 0.15 but lower bounds below 0.15, so they remain unresolved and active. H30 and H32 similarly suggest concentrated feature_003 effects among feature_007-positive and feature_015-positive strata, but their intervals do not entirely clear the threshold. H31 is below the threshold point estimate and has a wide interval crossing zero, so it is deferred rather than actively pursued. H33 rejects the registered feature_010 negative-direction claim because its signed estimate is strongly negative, implying the opposite raw association: feature_010 positivity is associated with a higher outcome_001 mean, i.e., weaker dependency, by roughly 0.42 units. I register a reversed feature_010 claim and, because feature_010 is a large unadjusted predictor, register stratified analyses to test whether feature_003 associations persist after excluding feature_010-positive individuals and whether the feature_010 association is consistent across feature_003 strata. The feature_053 level-10 versus level-5 contrast and the feature_011/014/006/021 probes are rejected or closed because their intervals do not support threshold-scale effects in the claimed directions. These are all unadjusted discovery associations; acceptance of H27 does not imply causality, biological interpretation, or confounding control.",
  "research_notes": "Current status: H27 accepted provisionally as dataset-specific evidence. It claims feature_003 positivity lowers outcome_001 within high feature_036; R21 signed estimate 0.443, interval 0.284 to 0.601, entirely above the 0.15 threshold. H27 validation requested now because it is the strongest candidate and subgroup multiplicity/selection are important concerns. H26 and H25 remain unresolved active; feature_003 may have related high-signature effects but lower bounds are below threshold. H30 and H32 remain unresolved active; H31 deferred due point below threshold and imprecision. H33 rejected: feature_010 positive is strongly associated with higher outcome_001, opposite the original direction, by about 0.42 units. New priorities: run reversed feature_010 main effect; test feature_003 overall and in key feature_003 subgroups restricted to feature_010=0; test feature_010 within feature_003=1 and feature_003=0. This will separate feature_003 and feature_010 associations or reveal confounding/stratification. Broad nulls: feature_053 level 10 vs 5, feature_011, feature_014, feature_006, feature_021, and many earlier marker/main probes. Do not interpret feature_003 signature subgroup effects as biological mechanisms; feature_038/018/036 are arbitrary standardized assays. If H27 validation fails, reconsider H27 and possibly the entire feature_003 high-signature cluster. If feature_003 effects disappear when feature_010=0, shift focus toward feature_010 as the more important predictor.",
